nitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-011\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"States that reserved items remain on the pickup shelf indefinitely until the Member cancels, conflicting with SD-011 which expires and cancels uncollected holds after 72 hours.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Chained 'and/or' operators leave it ambiguous which combination of the three actions is mandatory versus optional when an item is 7 days overdue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without identifying which human role or system component is responsible for reviewing, approving, and recording fine waiver requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the weak, subjective qualifier 'if appropriate' without defining the criteria for sending SMS due-date alerts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"before the due date if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify how far in advance (numeric duration and unit) of the due date the SMS alerts must be dispatched, and omits the concrete trigger condition behind 'if appropriate'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"for TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The retention period for payment receipts is left as an unresolved placeholder ('TBD years').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Charges $1.25 USD per overdue day with no maximum cap, conflicting with SD-019 which sets the overdue fine at $0.50 USD per day capped at $20.00 USD per item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"permitted to renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-020\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Allows Members to renew items regardless of unpaid overdue fines, directly contradicting SD-020 which blocks renewals when unpaid fines exceed $5.00 USD.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Patron's active loan count and enforce the 5-item borrowing limit on the Patron profile screen\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\",\n        \"SD-009\",\n        \"SD-015\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Introduces the inconsistent term 'Patron' instead of 'Member' used throughout earlier requirements (e.g., SD-001, SD-009), and also cites the 5-item limit from SD-009 which conflicts with the 8-item limit in SD-015.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"return search results quickly even when many users are querying\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms ('quickly', 'many users') without concrete latency or concurrency targets.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the non-committal escape phrase 'where possible', leaving it unclear when query term highlighting is required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient ISBN matching accuracy and acceptable response times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective terms ('sufficient', 'acceptable') without defining measurable accuracy percentages or response-time thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently process large batch MARC21 files without noticeable system slowdown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague, unmeasurable terms ('efficiently', 'large', 'noticeable system slowdown') with no concrete file size, throughput, or degradation thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"States that the Catalog Service shall detect active loans or holds on deletion attempts, but omits what action must follow detection (e.g., blocking deletion or returning an error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The backup execution schedule is left as an unresolved placeholder ('TBD intervals').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important administrative actions in a timely manner and retain them for an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague, undefined phrases ('important', 'in a timely manner', 'appropriate period') without specifying which actions, latency bounds, or retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Failover Manager shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"When the primary database node becomes unreachable, the requirement only specifies logging 'FAILOVER-01' and omits the actual failover behavior (e.g., promoting a standby node or rerouting traffic).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate transport security and clear error messages\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective terms ('adequate', 'clear') without specifying required protocols, cipher suites, or error message criteria.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"accept any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Accepts any password of at least 8 characters, conflicting with SD-002 which requires a minimum of 12 characters plus uppercase, lowercase, and numeric characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"active for 60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Keeps web portal sessions active for 60 minutes of inactivity, conflicting with SD-004 which terminates sessions after 15 minutes of inactivity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so Administrators can decrypt and retrieve forgotten passwords\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Requires reversible AES-256 encryption so passwords can be decrypted, conflicting with SD-003 which mandates one-way bcrypt hashing and prohibits storing or exposing plaintext passwords.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":76.44384,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":13604,"output_tokens":17940,"thinking_tokens":14740,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":31544}}}
